ash-on-hand edge over Kevin Lincoln", "Redistricting added Democratic-leaning Stockton to CA-13, improving Gray's terrain", "Expert ratings cluster at Likely/Lean D and markets price a Democratic win at 93-97%", "No public general-election polling, leaving the picture dependent on fundamentals"], "rationale": "Gray combines incumbency, a roughly two-to-one cash advantage and a redrawn district that now includes Stockton, and expert raters converge on a Democratic edge even where a few are cautious at Lean or Tilt D. Markets price a Democratic win around 93-97 percent, so the forecast sits at a mid-to-high single-digit Democratic margin with elevated uncertainty from the absence of polling.", "watch": "Any polling showing Lincoln within single digits, a surge in Republican outside spending, or a late shift in the national environment could push the race toward tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Adam Gray (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Adam Gray, the Democratic incumbent, faces Republican Kevin Lincoln, a former mayor, in a Central Valley district redrawn to include Stockton. Gray holds a clear financial edge, having raised about $4.2 million to Lincoln's $2.2 million, and enters the fall with roughly $2.1 million on hand versus $840,000. Outside spending has been minimal on both sides. No public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals, expert ratings and market pricing.\n\nRaters lean Democratic across the board, with most calling the race Likely or Safe Democratic and a few, including Cook Political Report and Inside Elections, more cautious at Lean or Tilt Democratic. Prediction markets put Democratic odds around 93 to 97 percent. The district's slight Democratic lean, Gray's incumbency and a favorable national environment point to a Democratic win in the mid-to-high single digits or low double digits, though the lack of polling leaves real uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9502, "margin": 10.95}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9343, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.945, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.941, "margin": 10.5}]}